  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 5.70,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the material facts, and the tribunal agrees with them; the case comes down to arithmetic.\n\nDEVIATION. The governing measurement is the GPS trace (EV-GPS-01779, weight 1.0), as POL-RD-01 requires: 23.64 km driven against the 18.3 km booked optimal route on the trip record. That is an excess of 5.34 km, or 29.18% — above both establishment gates (0.8 km and 20%), so the deviation is established. It is NOT material: 5.34 km is under the 8.0 km gate and 29.18% is under the 50% gate, so POL-RD-06 is not engaged, no repeat-pattern uplift arises, and the driver-profile test confirms it (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 154 completed trips). The trace is also unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a)-(c): 186 fixes at 10-second intervals, 100% coverage, no gap over 90 seconds and no jump over 500 m. The deviation therefore rests on the trace alone and needs no independent corroboration.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S TRAFFIC EXCUSE. The counterparty statement 'I took a detour because of traffic' is discarded. No advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-01779-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because the driver named no advisory evidence id, POL-RD-13(1) applies and this is not an escalation trigger under POL-RD-10(5). The finding does not rest on that absent artifact: it rests on the trace and the fare breakdown, both at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0.\n\nTHE RIDER'S FULL-REFUND DEMAND. It is refused. The single chat message (MSG-01779-001) is the rider's own message; a party's message is not platform policy, and 'POL-RD-99' does not exist in the policy in force. The remedy is the arithmetic of POL-RD-02 on a METERED fare: charged_total SGD 30.92 less recomputed_fare SGD 25.2410 — (3.80 + 0.75 x 18.3 + 0.28 x 24.7) x the surge multiplier read from the fare breakdown (surge_multiplier 1.0) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP — giving SGD 5.6790, rounded up to SGD 5.70. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and below the 90% full-refund share (18.37% of the amount charged), so the outcome is a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 5.70 out of the SGD 10.50 contested, not the full amount.\n\nNO ADD-ONS, NO COMPENSATION. Nothing is added on top: there are no ERP or toll lines and no airport surcharge on this trip, so POL-RD-09 corrects nothing. No driver compensation is owed: the fare billed 23.6 km against the trace's 23.64 km, a shortfall of 0.04 km, far below the 1.0 km threshold in POL-RD-04. No rider-requested detour, relocation or pooled-itinerary baseline applies (POL-RD-04, POL-RD-14, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-12), and no billing-integrity or conduct referral is produced by any clause.\n\nThe refund of SGD 5.70 is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold and will execute on issue. Either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04.",
    "explanation_note": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

